## UI/UX Standards & Documentation

**NAJWYŻSZE ŹRÓDŁO UI/UX:** `docs/ui-standards/CONSULTIFY_UI_UX_GOLDEN_STANDARD.md`

**OPERACYJNE ŹRÓDŁO DLA CURSOR:** `docs/ui-standards/CONSULTIFY_UI_UX_OPERATING_STANDARD.md`

**KANONICZNE ŹRÓDŁO:** `docs/ui-standards/README.md`

**⚠️ NIE WYMYŚLAJ NOWYCH STANDARDÓW ANI KOMPONENTÓW.** Wszystkie komponenty UI MUSZĄ być zgodne z dokumentacją w `docs/ui-standards/`. Jeśli standard nie opisuje przypadku — ZAPYTAJ, nie wymyślaj.

Core rule: feature screens do not own visual design. Feature screens compose approved Consultify layout and UI components. For all UI/UX work, first read `CONSULTIFY_UI_UX_GOLDEN_STANDARD.md`, then `CONSULTIFY_UI_UX_OPERATING_STANDARD.md`, then the detailed canonical standard they reference.

Before modifying any UI components:

1. **Read the documentation** — standards are in `docs/ui-standards/`:
   - `CONSULTIFY_UI_UX_GOLDEN_STANDARD.md` — highest UI/UX SSOT, DBR77 Tech Sexy 2027, Menu 2/3, N-mode, tables, timeline
   - `CONSULTIFY_UI_UX_OPERATING_STANDARD.md` — operating standard for Cursor/refactors
   - `UI_UX_MIGRATION_AUDIT.md` — current migration debt and target patterns
   - `UI_UX_MIGRATION_PLAN.md` — migration waves and component approval gates
   - `UI_UX_REFERENCE_SCREENS.md` — approved/candidate reference screens
   - `README.md` — index wszystkiego
   - `01-shell-layout/presentation-modes.md` — architecture D/N/C, N blocks kit
   - `01-shell-layout/n-mode-card-standard.md` — SSOT kart roboczych N-mode, AI affordance, visibility, katalog kart
   - `02-components/shared-sections.md` — NModeSections (Comments, Activity, Risk, Governance, Attachments)
   - `02-components/building-blocks.md` — NModeBlocks (Callout, ToggleBlock, EmptyState, Checklist, InlineTable, EmbeddedView)

2. **Use shared components** — NEVER duplicate UI code:
   - `src/components/shared/NModeSections/` — CommentsCanvas, ActivityLogCanvas, AttachmentsLinksCanvas, RiskCanvas, GovernanceCanvas
   - `src/components/shared/NModeBlocks/` — Callout, ToggleBlock, EmptyStateInline, ChecklistBlock, InlineTable, EmbeddedView
   - `src/components/shared/NModeLayout/` — NModeShell, NModeHeader, NModeLeftNav, NModeCanvas, NModePropertiesStrip
   - `src/components/shared/RowActionsMenu.tsx` — canonical table row `⋮` action menu with sections: Open → Tool Shortcut → Context → AI → Convert To → Create Output → Manage → Danger

3. **Follow naming conventions**: `{Section}Canvas.tsx` for shared sections
4. **Always support i18n**: PL + EN via `useTranslation`
5. **Always support locked state**: `locked?: boolean` prop for read-only artifacts

Table row actions:

- New App Table / ModuleHub row menus MUST use `RowActionsMenu`.
- Do not create custom row dropdowns in feature screens when `RowActionsMenu` can represent the menu.
- Keep vertical kebab `⋮` in the Actions column.
- Use the canonical section order from `docs/ui-standards/03-modules/app-table-standard.md`.
- `Delete` / `Usuń` is always last, red, and separated.

Table chips and badges:

- New App Table chips MUST follow `docs/ui-standards/03-modules/app-table-standard.md` (`StatusChip`, `PriorityChip`, `MetaChip`, `ToolChip`, `SlaChip` / `DueChip`).
- Metadata chips (tags/types/sources/tools) must stay neutral and readable in light/dark mode.
- Do not use primary/violet backgrounds as decorative metadata pills.
- Do not create multiple local color maps for the same chip semantics inside one module.

App Table color grid:

- New and migrated App Tables MUST use the enforced `Accepted App Table Color Grid` from `docs/ui-standards/00-foundation/color-system.md`.
- Do not create local table surface, separator, selected/focused/checked row, text, or chip color grids.
- Selected/focused rows must be immediately visible: brand `primary/violet-blue` tint, `4px` left accent, and visible inset ring.
- Do not use random cyan/amber/gray row-state colors for App Table selected/focused/checked states.

App Table column mechanics:

- New and migrated App Tables MUST follow the approved `My Work > Pomysły` golden reference in `docs/ui-standards/03-modules/app-table-standard.md`.
- New operational record lists in `My Work`, `Wywiad`, queues, sessions, templates, insights and initiatives MUST start from the App Table canon; do not create local card-list/table hybrids unless a compliant App Table view already exists.
- Column resize MUST behave like Excel boundaries: dragging a separator moves that separator; one adjacent column grows by the same amount the other adjacent column shrinks.
- Do not implement table resize as changing only one column and letting the browser recalculate the rest.
- App Tables must keep stable full-width layout (`table-fixed` or equivalent fixed column contract).
- `Title` / primary object must have a real width contract and a boundary resizer before the first metadata column.
- Metadata headers/cells are centered; `Title` remains left-aligned.
- Simple table column settings open as a compact anchored popover under the settings icon, not a modal.
- Do not show redundant `Actions/Akcje` text in the actions header when the table settings icon owns that corner.
- Row description/justification is visible by default under the primary title, uses the same neutral text family with lighter opacity/weight, and must not appear only on hover.
- Table settings popovers include a persisted `Pokaż opis / uzasadnienie` / `Show row description` checkbox at the bottom instead of a simple reset button in lightweight tables.
- If row descriptions are hidden, keep calm row padding; do not collapse rows into cramped spreadsheet density.

Detailed rules are in `.cursor/rules/nmode-shared-components.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/ui-standards-documentation.mdc`.

